# 🧬 Hierarchy-aware Medication Recommendation

[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/Python-3.10+-blue.svg)](https://python.org)
[![PyTorch](https://img.shields.io/badge/PyTorch-2.0+-red.svg)](https://pytorch.org)
[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-green.svg)](LICENSE)

> Integrating patient EHR data with drug molecular structure for ATC hierarchy-aware multi-label drug recommendation.
> 
> *Improves accuracy, interpretability, and clinical consistency through multimodal fusion and hierarchical modeling.*

---

## 📌 You need to know first!

| Branch | Purpose |
|:-------|:--------|
| `main` | Full implementation with hierarchical ATC prediction + drug molecular fusion |
| `archived` | Legacy version for reproducing paper results |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Which branch to use?**
> - Use this branch (`main`) for learning and using the code
> - Use the [archived branch](https://github.com/ycq091044/SafeDrug/tree/archived) to reproduce paper results

> [!NOTE]
> **Implementation differences from paper:**
> 1. Drug SMILES strings: paper's crawling method missed many molecules; current branch uses **DrugBank method** for more comprehensive coverage
> 2. Data preprocessing script differs → output statistics may vary from paper

---

## ✨ Highlights

| Feature | Description |
|:--------|:------------|
| 🏥 **Hierarchical ATC prediction** | L1 → L2 → L3 → L4 |
| 💊 **Cross-attention drug knowledge fusion** | Multimodal integration |
| ⚖️ **4-layer defense for class imbalance** | Robust handling |
| 🎯 **Performance** | F1 = 0.70, Jaccard = 0.55 on MIMIC-III |

